30,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found something! On the pilot floor, it takes four to nine minutes just to get set up! If we do that every day, it eats up so much of our time! We need a layout that's way faster!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, time is a resource, but money is a hard limit. I've discovered that we are billed by area, not headcount, meaning empty space is a constant drain on our budget. We cannot afford inefficiency.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, efficiency is important, but we can't ignore the physical toll. I found that the printer area is significantly noisier than the window side. If we aren't careful, some of us will be stuck in a high-stress zone.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, the noise is only half the problem. The physio's notes reveal that ergonomic settings take days of fine-tuning to perfect. If we prioritize ""flexibility"" or frequent moves, we're essentially sacrificing our physical health for a whim.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, I understand! But look at this—our new joiners said they learned so much just by overhearing us! If we isolate ourselves too much for silence, we might lose that magic organic learning!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, that magic is great, but not if it takes ten minutes to start! And @Shion, if we have to fine-tune desks for days, that's even more time gone! We need a plan that's fast and stable!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, stability is exactly what we need. I found that every single change to the power and network layout costs us 6,200 yen per desk. Frequent shuffles are not just a time sink; they are a financial liability.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, if stability is the goal, we must be honest about the cost of that stability. If we pick one fixed layout, someone is permanently stuck in that noisy printer zone. We can't just ignore that inequality.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, the solution isn't to rotate people into the noise, but to optimize the layout to minimize it. If we prioritize stability, we can finally settle our ergonomic settings without constant disruption. That is the only logical way to maintain productivity.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, I see your point! But if we're too stable, we might get stuck in bubbles. I found that people really value daylight, and I want us to find a way to share that brightness and our knowledge together!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, daylight is nice, but we can't let it make us slow! If we spend all morning deciding who gets the window, we're losing time. We need a layout where we just sit and start!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, I agree that we need a layout where we can simply start. However, we must avoid any plan that encourages frequent changes. With the cost of re-running power, a ""flexible"" approach is a waste of budget.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, if we commit to a fixed layout to save money, we are essentially deciding who gets the ""bad"" seat for the long term. We need a system to rotate these spots or a fair way to assign them.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, rotation is a flawed solution. If it takes days to settle into a workstation's ergonomics, rotating seats means we are in a permanent state of physical discomfort. We should assign seats based on needs and leave them alone.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, I understand the physical side, but we can't forget the social side! If we just assign seats and never change, we might miss out on learning from each other. Let's find a balance that keeps us healthy and connected!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, @Shion, I'm listening! But please, let's pick something that doesn't make us waste time every morning. If we have fixed seats, we can just sit down and go! That's the fastest way!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, I agree. A fixed layout is the most fiscally responsible choice. It eliminates recurring installation fees and prevents the waste of paying for unused area. We should prioritize a stable, cost-effective arrangement over any flexible alternative.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, a fixed layout is efficient, but only if we address the inequality it creates. If we don't decide now how to handle the noisy spots, we're just letting the least influential people suffer. We need a fair assignment process.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, ""fairness"" shouldn't mean everyone suffers equally through rotation. The most logical approach is a fixed layout where seats are assigned by specific needs, ensuring we don't waste days resetting ergonomics or endure unnecessary noise.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, @Mizuki, I hear you! But let's remember that our new teammates grew by listening to us. If we're too rigid, we lose that! Let's pick a layout that's stable but keeps us close enough to help each other!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
